Subject: [PATCH 0006/0014] Remove Live Share

Live Share ships no code in the OSS tree: no extension, no service,
no command, no walkthrough step references it. The only occurrences
are an API-proposal enum member, test data, and stock illustration
SVGs, none of which constitute the feature. There is therefore no
upstream hunk to carry; build.sh skips diff-less patches explicitly.

Enforcement lands in patch 0008: with the marketplace pointed at
Open VSX, the proprietary Live Share extension is uninstallable.

Rationale: single-user workspaces have no real-time collaboration
scope, and Live Share is proprietary.

Verification: patch regression test fails without it and passes with it.
